# Excalibur GN build flags.
#
# One `name=value` per line. build.py merges this file over the upstream flags:
# a flag upstream already sets is replaced, anything else is appended.
#
# Upstream (upstream/ungoogled-chromium-windows/ungoogled-chromium/flags.gn and
# flags.windows.gn) already sets the privacy-relevant flags, including:
#   safe_browsing_mode=0, enable_reporting=false, enable_mdns=false,
#   enable_remoting=false, enable_service_discovery=false,
#   enable_hangout_services_extension=false, google_api_key="",
#   use_official_google_api_keys=false, disable_fieldtrial_testing_config=true
#
# Only add a flag here after confirming it exists in the pinned Chromium
# version: the build runs `gn gen --fail-on-unused-args`, so an unknown flag
# fails the build.
